      "note": "Proxy for an Indian bank fixed-deposit / RBI-era regulated deposit rate: RBI's published '1 to 3 years' scheduled-commercial-bank term deposit rate (RBI Handbook of Statistics, Table 'Structure of Interest Rates'), using the midpoint of the published rate range for each RBI fiscal year (April-March) and mapping the fiscal-year-end (March) observation to that calendar year. Solidly documented, non-interpolated anchor years: 1981, 1982, 1986, 1988, 1992, 1993, 1995-2001, 2005-2023 (fiscal years 2004-05 through 2022-23), 2024 and 2025 (current SBI 1-year retail term deposit card rate, ~6.8% in 2024 easing to 6.25% by late 2025). India's bank deposit rates were administratively regulated/capped (not market-set) until full deregulation in October 1997; the 1980-2003 window mixes a hard ceiling era (pre-1992), a single 13% ceiling (1992-94), the 10%/12% ceiling revisions (1994-96), and full deregulation (from Oct 1997) - this is reflected in the anchor values. Years 1980, 1983-1985, 1987, 1989-1991, 1994, 2002-2004 have NO direct published RBI rate found for that exact calendar year and are LINEARLY INTERPOLATED between the nearest documented anchor years (or flat-extended for 1980, before the first anchor). Treat dataQuality='estimated' accordingly; this is a materially rougher series than the US Treasury-bill series in us.json."
